  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">EJASA 2</narrative>
  </title>
  <description akvo:type="3" type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">12,500 youngs (m/f) working in agriculture in northern Benin</narrative>
  </description>
  <description akvo:type="5" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">EJASA 2 is a young employment project in the food-agri sector with the aim to, increase revenue, improve food security/nutrition and contribute to social resillience. 

Around 12.500 young people, 50% of whom are women, will participate. The project will run from 2023 to 2027 and is implemented in the departments of Alibori and Atacora of North Benin. The targeted sectors are market gardening, soybeans, poultry and the breeding of small ruminants such as goats and sheep.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description akvo:type="4" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Emploi des Jeunes pour une Am&#xE9;lioration de la S&#xE9;curit&#xE9; Alimentaire au Nord B&#xE9;nin</narrative>
  </description>
  <description akvo:type="9" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">In northern Benin, the populations of the Atacora and Alibori departments are faced with a number of difficulties, including their limited ability to meet their food and nutritional needs due to low agricultural productivity and widespread poverty. The concern for young people, whose prospects for integration are limited and whose numbers are increasing rapidly, is greater because of their poor access to resources. These factors are compounded by growing insecurity and violent extremism.

This is why SNV has been implementing the &quot;Youth Employment for the Improvement of Food Security in Northern Benin (EJASA)&quot; project since October 15, 2020.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description akvo:type="8" type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Increase revenue of young people (50% women)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description akvo:type="6" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Scheduled for twenty-seven (27) months, the pilot project (EJASA 1) is funded by the Embassy of the Kingdom of the Netherlands near Benin. It aims to increase the incomes and productivity of 4,250 young people (men and women) working in agriculture through climate-resilient agricultural management and a more inclusive and favorable institutional environment.

EJASA 2 is a 15mil, 5 years project to increase the revenue of approximately 12500 youngs. The project started since January 15, 2023, aims at contributing to improving the security situation and social stability in Benin by providing meaningful employment opportunities for young people and improving the food security of communities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description akvo:type="10" type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">To ensure the sustainability and extent of the project&apos;s impacts, partnerships and synergies will be created with a variety of public and private actors; young people will be encouraged to develop solidarity and peer support mechanisms. The expected benefits will obviously be at the level of the young participants, and more broadly at the level of their families. To assure the efficiency and effectiveness of the project special attention will be given to learning with innovative instruments such as AAER, MSC, SenseMaker and Social Network Analysis.</narrative>
  </description>
